### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Welcome & Route Overview
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. View All Users (Verifies passwords are encrypted as bcrypt hashes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Register a New User - Success (200 OK)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ayyappa",
  "name": "Ayyappa Sonti",
  "password": "ayyappa@secure2026",
  "gender": "Male",
  "location": "Hyderabad"
}

### 4. Register - Failure: Duplicate Username (400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ayyappa",
  "name": "Ayyappa Sonti",
  "password": "anotherpassword",
  "gender": "Male",
  "location": "Hyderabad"
}

### 5. Register - Failure: Password Too Short (< 5 chars) (400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "shortpass_user",
  "name": "Short Pass User",
  "password": "123",
  "gender": "Male",
  "location": "Bengaluru"
}

### 6. Login - Success (200 OK, returns { jwt_token })
# @name loginSuccess
POST {{baseUrl}}/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ayyappa",
  "password": "ayyappa@secure2026"
}

### 7. Login - Failure: Unknown / Non-existent User (400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "unknown_ghost_user",
  "password": "somepassword"
}

### 8. Login - Failure: Wrong Password (400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ayyappa",
  "password": "wrong_password_xyz"
}

### 9. Access Protected Route with JWT Token
@token = {{loginSuccess.response.body.jwt_token}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/profile/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Access Protected Route without JWT Token (401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile/
